+      # THE TRADEOFF, ON THE RECORD: a re-verify does not run a fresh questioner+answerer pass, so
+      # a NEW problem introduced by a correction is not caught by the qa-review dimension on that
+      # round. That is deliberate. Every other gate signal IS re-derived from scratch on the new
+      # head — CI re-runs (`CI_STATUS`), the archon plan gate re-evaluates plan distance and calls
+      # an increase a regression (`PLAN_GATE`), and blis-pr-review re-reviews the whole diff
+      # (`AGENT_VERDICT`) — so a fix that breaks something is still gated three ways, just not by a
+      # second cross-vendor probe. That probe's distinctive value is on the ORIGINAL diff, where it
+      # catches what a single-vendor review missed; re-running it every round to re-scan a small
+      # correction costs a full questioner+answerer pass for coverage the three signals above
+      # already provide. What the re-verify DOES add is the thing those three cannot: a check that
